 Given the parameterized curve \((x, y) = (t^3 + 7, -3t^2 - 6t - 5)\), we need to find the coordinates of the curve at \(t = 2\). We simply substitute \(t = 2\) into the parameter equations for \(x\) and \(y\): \[
\begin{aligned}
x &= 2^3 + 7 = 8 + 7 = 15, \\
y &= -3(2^2) - 6(2) - 5 = -3(4) - 12 - 5 = -12 - 12 - 5 = -29.
\end{aligned}
\] So the point the curve passes through at \(t = 2\) is \((15, -29)\). </think> <answer> \((15, -29)\) </answer>

